Accept android-key attestation statements.

libfido2's cbor_decode_fmt allowlists four attestation formats and returns -1 for
anything else. Android made hardware-backed `android-key` the FIDO2 default in April
2025 with no opt-out, so every Android credential provider now fails to enrol through
libfido2 - the ceremony succeeds and then the response fails to parse, surfacing as
FIDO_ERR_INTERNAL.

Windows makes this unavoidable: libfido2's Hello backend hardcodes
dwAttestationConveyancePreference = DIRECT, so a caller cannot ask for no attestation.

android-key's statement is {alg, sig, x5c}, which decode_attstmt_entry already handles,
so accepting the format name is the whole fix. lokot never verifies attestation - it
uses only the credential id and the hmac-secret output - so nothing downstream depends
on the statement being understood.

--- a/src/cbor.c
+++ b/src/cbor.c
@@ -943,8 +943,9 @@
 		return (-1);
 	}

-	if (strcmp(type, "packed") && strcmp(type, "fido-u2f") &&
-	    strcmp(type, "none") && strcmp(type, "tpm")) {
+	if (strcmp(type, "packed") && strcmp(type, "fido-u2f") &&
+	    strcmp(type, "none") && strcmp(type, "tpm") &&
+	    strcmp(type, "android-key")) {
 		fido_log_debug("%s: type=%s", __func__, type);
 		free(type);
 		return (-1);
